&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a dedicated Home Health Aid to work in Washington Crossing on Friday, Saturday and Sunday overnights. We are offering 20$ an hour. Hope you can help! Here is some information about our client below-&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;92&quot; data-end=&quot;303&quot;&gt;Male- is a 47-year-old male residing in Washington Crossing with his parents. He sustained a spinal cord injury in 2018 following a diving accident, resulting in quadriplegia with partial use of his right arm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;305&quot; data-end=&quot;596&quot;&gt;Ryan requires assistance with activities of daily living. He uses PRN oxygen, takes medications orally, and eats by mouth. He has a suprapubic catheter in place and requires the use of a mechanical lift for all transfers. Once transferred, he is able to independently operate his wheelchair.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;598&quot; data-end=&quot;720&quot;&gt;Ryan is alert, oriented, and able to effectively communicate his needs. He is actively involved in directing his own care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;722&quot; data-end=&quot;778&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-start=&quot;722&quot; data-end=&quot;778&quot;&gt;Please note: Client is 6’3” and approximately 280 lbs.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
